 "contract_id": "case-p19.actinv-self-shielding",
 "revision": 2,
 "status": "draft",
 "question": "On the frozen TENDL-2025 test set {W-186, Ag-107, Ta-181, Nb-93, U-238, Fe-56}, do ACTINV's deterministic unresolved-range Bondarenko tables agree with independent NJOY2016.79 PURR (node level) and GROUPR (FISPACT-709 group level) processing within the measured tolerances, and does every declared material appear in the emitted table?",
 "assumptions": [
  "The six ENDF-6 evaluation files are the frozen TENDL-2025 test set; Core verifies byte identity by digest and does not qualify the evaluation physics.",
  "NJOY2016.79 is an independent processing oracle executed through a pinned interpreter driver; its Monte Carlo ladders are stochastic, so oracle rows carry sampling noise that the declared tolerance must absorb. ACTINV's production path never invokes NJOY.",
  "ACTINV's shield table is produced by the deterministic stratified-quantile PURR-equivalent processor in actinv build-shielding; the table artifact is verified by digest.",
  "The comparison covers unresolved-range (MF=2 LRU=2) Bondarenko factors for the declared sigma0 x temperature grid only. Resolved-resonance pointwise shielding and probability-table transport are outside the question.",
  "This contract is an internal development feedback case, not a release qualification.",
  "GROUPR applies the pointwise Bondarenko weight across each full group; partially-covered groups whose uncovered sliver contains resolved resonances include suppression ACTINV does not claim, so the group gate applies to fully-covered groups and partial groups are reported.",
  "The group qualification metric is the full-group Bondarenko fold (group_factors), which weights the covered segment by its probability-table flux and the uncovered part by sigma0/(sigma0+background); the flat lethargy blend is retained only as a legacy fallback."
 ],
